<!--
  <sui-tree-grid> — engine-backed hierarchical TREE-GRID (role=treegrid).

  The SAME flattened depth-first `tree.rows()` from the REUSED Table engine
  (createTable with getSubRows+expanded — NO createTree()), rendered through
  the Table view's COLUMN/CELL machinery (row.getVisibleCells()), with the
  disclosure caret + indent in the FIRST visible column. navMode:'cell' (vs
  'row' for sui-tree); role=treegrid (vs role=tree). The live Table<T>
  (carrying the column defs) arrives via prop:tree IDENTITY binding; a
  nodes+columns JSON pair is the SSR fallback.

  Density is the platform axis (<html data-density>). NO density/dense prop.

  Events (host.emit): sui-toggle {id, expanded}, sui-expand-change {expanded},
  sui-select {id}, sui-node-select {selected, selectedIds}, sui-node-click
  {id, depth, index}.

  Anatomy (anatomy = the dom structure the controller renders into shadow;
  every named part has a `part=` attribute the test selectors pin to, and
  every styling class below is a LINT-DISALLOWED public hook — tests anchor
  on `part=` / `data-*` / `role=`, not on class names):

    <sui-tree-grid>            shadow root
      ├─ .grid    part=grid    <column>, role=treegrid (the tablegrid)
      │   ├─ .head part=thead  sticky header row, role=row
      │   │   └─ .col-head    part=columnheader, role=columnheader (×N)
      │   │       ├─ .col-label            (text)
      │   │       ├─ .sort-glyph  sui-icon chevron-up|down (when sorted)
      │   │       ├─ <button>   data-action=column-menu, ghost xs (when canHide)
      │   │       └─ .resize-handle part=resize-handle (when canResize)
      │   └─ .viewport part=viewport
      │       └─ .spacer part=spacer (the virtualizer total-size ruler)
      │           └─ .row     part=row, role=row (per visible row)
      │               └─ .cell part=cell, role=gridcell (per visible column)
      │                   ├─ .caret  part=caret, sui-icon chevron-right
      │                   └─ .cell-label (text)
      ├─ .tree-error part=error (sui-error-state inside, when error attr)
      └─ .tree-empty part=empty (sui-empty-state inside, when no rows)

  Columns arrive on the live `Table<T>` via the `prop:tree` identity host
  property; `nodes`/`columns` JSON pair is the SSR fallback.

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from feat/next, parity-gate pass)
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - tone is NOT a prop on this component — the spike's prior <theme
    prop="tone"> block was deleted. There is no tone/size channel
    scaffolding for this component; size IS a prop (sm/md/lg) but it is
    not used for visual treatment here (density is the platform axis,
    not a per-component switch — feat/next never re-declared density
    per instance).
  - The outer container is a <column> (layout primitive) carrying the
    sx surface — the closed sx vocab (tokens only) handles the rounded
    surface, the border, the overflow, and the bg. The "grid" layout
    itself is a flex column with the head/row grid-template set per
    render via inline style:--sui-grid-template (sx cannot drive
    grid-template-columns, see "stays in <style>" below).
  - The column-menu control is a bare framework <button ghost xs>. No
    hand-styled .col-menu (no display/color/hover/border-radius
    authored here). The control-skin fix the alert pilot surfaced
    (adoptSuiSheets now carries CONTROL_SKINS_CSS) means a ghost
    button inside this shadow L2 paints correctly.
  - sx is closed-vocabulary. Everything else sx structurally cannot
    express stays in <style>: per-element layout (display:grid/flex on
    semantic elements — replacing these with <row>/<column> would
    add wrapping semantics and break the cell/caret grid behavior),
    the --sui-grid-template dynamic var (per-render from the engine's
    column-sizing lane), the .row absolute positioning + per-window
    translateY transform (the virtualizer's offset bookkeeping), the
    sticky .head with z-index, the .row[data-expanded] .caret rotate
    + .row:not([data-can-expand]) .caret visibility-hidden (descendant
    attribute selectors — variants only target .sui-tree-grid attrs), the
    .col-head[data-sortable] cursor/hover, the .row[data-selected]
    ::before primary marker, the .row:focus-visible inset box-shadow
    ring, the multi-property transitions, the cell/head color/border/
    text-transform/white-space/user-select, and the @media (forced-
    colors) CanvasText outline.
  - The feat/next baseline's .sui-tree-grid { font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--density-text) } lives in <style> — no sx prop for
    font-family, and --density-text is a runtime density variable,
    not a token (it's set by the platform density axis at <html>).
  - The empty-state's "Clear filters" action was already a bare
    <button> in feat/next — kept as-is, no L1-control changes needed.
  - Tests pin to part= / data-* / role=, NOT to .col-menu or .col-label
    or .cell — anatomy is class-free for the public hooks; the .col-*
    and .cell classes are private styling hooks only.

  No new LANG-GAP. The control-skin fix the alert pilot surfaced is in
  place; <button ghost xs> here paints correctly inside this shadow L2.
-->

<component>{
  props: {
    nodes: '',
    columns: '',
    label: '',
    selectable: 'none' | 'single' | 'multi',
    'expand-on-select': false,
    size: 'md' | 'sm' | 'lg',
    loading: false,
    error: '',
  },
}</component>
<style>
  /* The dynamic grid-template track string is set per-render by the
   * controller via style:--sui-grid-template={…} (an inline custom-
   * property attribute on the .grid element). The lint cannot see
   * those, so we declare the var locally with a sane default that
   * matches the per-render expression's first-frame value. Same for
   * --sui-col-count, which the controller sets on the same element
   * and the .head/.row reference directly. */
  .sui-tree-grid { --sui-grid-template: repeat(1, minmax(80px, 1fr)); }

  .sui-tree-grid {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--density-text);
    --sui-tree-indent: var(--density-row-px);
    --sui-col-count: 1;
  }

  .head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--sui-grid-template);
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: var(--z-sticky);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 0 var(--border);
  }
  .col-head {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: var(--density-row-py) var(--density-row-px);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--foreground);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    white-space: nowrap;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .col-head[data-sortable] { cursor: pointer; }
  .col-head[data-sortable]:hover { color: var(--foreground); }
  .col-head .sort-glyph {
    display: inline-flex;
    color: var(--primary);
  }
  .col-head .col-label { flex: 1; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .col-head [data-action='column-menu'] {
    width: var(--density-icon);
    height: var(--density-icon);
    padding: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    /* The ghost button is already inline-flex centered; the size-channel
     * min-height would otherwise override --density-icon. Force the
     * density-icon to win so the menu trigger lines up with the sort
     * glyph + caret. The control-skin fix carries the hover wash. */
  }
  .resize-handle {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block: 0;
    inset-inline-end: 0;
    width: var(--space-1);
    cursor: col-resize;
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .resize-handle:hover { background: var(--primary); }

  .viewport {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    overflow-y: auto;
    max-height: 480px;
  }
  .spacer { position: relative; width: 100%; }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--sui-grid-template);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    cursor: pointer;
    outline: none;
    transition: background-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .row:hover { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  .row[data-selected] {
    background: var(--selected-bg);
  }
  .row[data-selected]::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0; top: 4px; bottom: 4px;
    width: 3px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background: var(--primary);
  }
  .row:focus-visible { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 var(--ring-width) var(--ring-color); }

  .cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--density-row-gap);
    padding: var(--density-row-py) var(--density-row-px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    color: var(--foreground);
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .caret {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex: none;
    width: var(--density-icon);
    height: var(--density-icon);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .row[data-expanded] .caret { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  .row:not([data-can-expand]) .caret { visibility: hidden; }

  .cell-label {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .row:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid CanvasText; outline-offset: -2px; }
  }

  .sui-tree-grid[hidden] { display: none; }
</style>


<controller>
// <sui-tree-grid> controller — the SAME engine-backed flattened tree, rendered
// through Table's column/cell machinery (role=treegrid, navMode:'cell').
//
// REUSES createTable (getSubRows+expanded) + createVirtualizer; NO createTree().
// Differs from `sui-tree` only in navMode/role/render: it reads the same
// flattened `tree.rows()` but maps each row's `getVisibleCells()` into cells
// (the disclosure caret + indent land in the FIRST visible column). Columns
// arrive on the live `Table<T>` via the `prop:tree` identity host property; a
// `nodes`/`columns` JSON pair is the SSR fallback.
//
// Authority: build-spec §"The view", §"sui-tree-grid", Slice 5; behavioral #8.

import { controller, signal, derived, ref } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import type { ViewScope } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import { createVirtualizer, type Virtual } from '@ship/sui-runtime/virtual'
import { createTable, type Table } from '../sui-table/engine/create-table'
import type { TreeNode } from '../sui-tree-view/sui-tree-view.controller'
import { parseJsonColumns, parseJsonNodes } from '../sui-tree/decode'
import { treeTableOptions } from '../sui-tree/sui-tree.engine'
import { treeHeaderViews, windowTreeRows, type TreeHeaderView } from '../sui-tree/sui-tree.view'
import { wireTreeInteractions } from '../sui-tree/sui-tree.interactions'
import { wireGridColumns } from './sui-tree-grid.columns'
import type { Scope } from './sui-tree-grid.sui'

type AnyTreeNode = TreeNode & Record<string, unknown>

const INDENT_STEP = 16
const ROW_HEIGHT = 32

function emptyTree(): Table<AnyTreeNode> {
  return createTable<AnyTreeNode>(treeTableOptions<AnyTreeNode>({ data: [], navMode: 'cell' }))
}

export default controller({
  // `nodes`/`columns` (string) + `selectable` (enum) are read imperatively from
  // the host — they are not part of the compiler-emitted `Scope`.
  scope: (_ctx: ViewScope<Scope>) => {
    const treeSig = signal<Table<AnyTreeNode> | null>(null)
    const viewportEl = ref<HTMLDivElement>(null)

    const EMPTY = emptyTree()
    const tree = derived<Table<AnyTreeNode>>(() => treeSig() ?? EMPTY)

    const virt: Virtual = createVirtualizer({
      count: () => tree().rows().length,
      estimateSize: (_index) => ROW_HEIGHT,
      getScrollElement: () => viewportEl(),
      overscan: 8,
      getItemKey: (i) => tree().rows()[i]?.id ?? i,
    })

    const headers = derived<TreeHeaderView[]>(() => treeHeaderViews(tree()))
    // The grid-template track string off the resolved per-column sizes — reflects
    // a resize (setColumnSizing) live so the rendered column widens. Empty cols
    // fall back to the equal-fraction default the CSS seeds.
    const gridTemplate = derived<string>(() => {
      const hs = headers()
      if (hs.length === 0) return 'minmax(80px, 1fr)'
      return hs.map((h) => h.size).join(' ')
    })
    const windowItems = windowTreeRows<AnyTreeNode>(tree, virt.virtualItems, () => INDENT_STEP)
    const totalSize = virt.totalSize
    const rowCount = derived<number>(() => tree().rowCount())

    const activeRowId = derived<string | null>(() => {
      const active = tree().nav.active().rowId
      if (active != null) return active
      return tree().rows()[0]?.id ?? null
    })

    const isEmptyInitial = derived<boolean>(
      () => tree().rows().length === 0 && !tree().hasActiveFilters(),
    )
    const isEmptyFiltered = derived<boolean>(
      () => tree().rows().length === 0 && tree().hasActiveFilters(),
    )

    return {
      treeSig,
      viewportEl,
      tree,
      virt,
      headers,
      gridTemplate,
      windowItems,
      totalSize,
      rowCount,
      activeRowId,
      isEmptyInitial,
      isEmptyFiltered,
    }
  },

  mount(state, host) {
    Object.defineProperty(host, 'tree', {
      configurable: true,
      get: () => state.tree,
      set: (t: Table<AnyTreeNode> | null) => {
        state.treeSig = t
      },
    })

    // SSR fallback: build an engine from `nodes` + `columns` JSON attributes.
    if (state.treeSig == null) {
      const rawNodes = (host as { nodes?: string }).nodes ?? host.getAttribute('nodes') ?? ''
      const rawCols = (host as { columns?: string }).columns ?? host.getAttribute('columns') ?? ''
      const parsedNodes = parseJsonNodes(rawNodes)
      const parsedCols = parseJsonColumns(rawCols)
      if (parsedNodes.length > 0 && parsedCols.length > 0) {
        const selAttr = host.getAttribute('selectable') ?? 'none'
        state.treeSig = createTable<AnyTreeNode>(
          treeTableOptions<AnyTreeNode>({
            data: parsedNodes as AnyTreeNode[],
            columns: parsedCols as never,
            navMode: 'cell',
            selectable: selAttr !== 'none',
            multiSelect: selAttr === 'multi',
          }),
        )
      }
    }

    const stop = wireTreeInteractions(host, () => state.tree, {
      expandOnSelect: () => host.hasAttribute('expand-on-select'),
      selectable: () => (host.getAttribute('selectable') ?? 'none') !== 'none',
      multi: () => (host.getAttribute('selectable') ?? 'none') === 'multi',
      navRoleSelector: '[role="treegrid"]',
      getWindow: () => state.$signals.windowItems(),
    })

    // The ORTHOGONAL column lane: header sort/hide + a pointer-drag resize route
    // through the REUSED engine's column mutators (no tree-specific column code).
    const stopColumns = wireGridColumns(host, () => state.tree)

    return () => {
      stop()
      stopColumns()
      state.virt.dispose()
    }
  },
})

</controller>
{#if error() !== ''}
<div sx="display:block w:full fg:foreground" class="tree-error error" role="alert">
  <error-state>{error()}</error-state>
</div>
{:else if isEmptyInitial()}
<div class="tree-empty empty" role="status">
  <slot name="empty"><empty-state></empty-state></slot>
</div>
{:else if isEmptyFiltered()}
<div class="tree-empty empty" role="status">
  <slot name="empty">
    <empty-state>
      <button slot="action" type="button" data-action="clear-filters">Clear filters</button>
    </empty-state>
  </slot>
</div>
{:else}
<column class="grid" role="treegrid" gap="0" aria-label={label() || null} aria-rowcount={rowCount()} aria-multiselectable={selectable() === 'multi' ? 'true' : null} style:--sui-col-count={headers().length} style:--sui-grid-template={gridTemplate()} sx="w:full overflow:hidden bg:surface-1 border:border radius:lg">
  <div class="head thead" role="row">
    {#for h of headers() key={h.id}}
      <div class="col-head columnheader" role="columnheader" data-col-id={h.id} data-sortable={h.canSort ? 'true' : null} data-sorted={h.sorted || null} aria-sort={h.canSort ? h.ariaSort : null}>
        <span class="col-label">{h.label}</span>
        {#if h.sorted === 'asc'}
          <span class="sort-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><icon name="chevron-up" size="xs"></icon></span>
        {:else if h.sorted === 'desc'}
          <span class="sort-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><icon name="chevron-down" size="xs"></icon></span>
        {/if}
        {#if h.canHide}
          <button class="column-menu" ghost xs type="button" data-action="column-menu" data-col-id={h.id} aria-label="Column options">
            <icon name="more-vertical" size="xs"></icon>
          </button>
        {/if}
        {#if h.canResize}
          <span class="resize-handle" data-col-id={h.id} aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {/if}
      </div>
    {/for}
  </div>
  <div class="viewport" bind:this={viewportEl}>
    <div class="spacer" style:height={`${totalSize()}px`}>
      {#for w of windowItems() key={`${w.key}|${w.cellsKey}`}}
        <div class="row" role="row" data-node-id={w.id} aria-level={w.level} aria-posinset={w.posInSet} aria-setsize={w.setSize} aria-rowindex={w.index + 1} aria-expanded={w.canExpand ? (w.expanded ? 'true' : 'false') : null} aria-selected={selectable() !== 'none' ? (w.selected ? 'true' : 'false') : null} data-can-expand={w.canExpand ? 'true' : null} data-expanded={w.expanded ? 'true' : null} data-selected={w.selected ? 'true' : null} tabindex={w.id === activeRowId() ? '0' : '-1'} style:transform={`translateY(${w.start}px)`}>
          {#for c of w.cells key={c.columnId}}
            <div class="cell" role="gridcell" style:padding-inline-start={c.first ? `calc(var(--density-row-px) + ${w.indent}px)` : null}>
              {#if c.first && w.canExpand}
                <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true">
                  <icon name="chevron-right" size="xs"></icon>
                </span>
              {/if}
              <span class="cell-label">{c.value}</span>
            </div>
          {/for}
        </div>
      {/for}
    </div>
  </div>
</column>
{/if}
